1
00:00:04,030 --> 00:00:06,869
Did you not hear me?
I said to let me pass.

2
00:00:06,870 --> 00:00:09,239
I have no business
with you, Assassin.

3
00:00:09,240 --> 00:00:12,750
And did you not hear me when I
said to force your way through?

4
00:00:13,250 --> 00:00:16,710
If you do not hurry, your
Master's life will be forfeit.

5
00:00:18,250 --> 00:00:21,510
Don't be so angry
at Assassin, Caster.

6
00:00:22,010 --> 00:00:24,299
He faces Saber.

7
00:00:24,300 --> 00:00:26,969
I don't know who
that samurai is,

8
00:00:26,970 --> 00:00:30,099
but he must be a master swordsman
indeed to hold Saber at bay.

9
00:00:30,100 --> 00:00:32,140
Shouldn't you be
complimenting him instead?

10
00:00:33,430 --> 00:00:35,020
Surely you jest.

11
00:00:35,350 --> 00:00:39,270
I could hardly consider him a hero
if he failed to stop the likes of you.

12
00:00:39,610 --> 00:00:44,109
That man lacks the skill to call
himself a master swordsman.

13
00:00:44,110 --> 00:00:45,860
Saber is here?

14
00:00:59,210 --> 00:01:04,250
In the face of absolute despair

15
00:01:04,550 --> 00:01:08,250
That nearly burned
our hearts away

16
00:01:09,750 --> 00:01:14,800
You still found the
courage to smile

17
00:01:15,050 --> 00:01:19,600
Like you accepted it all

18
00:01:20,400 --> 00:01:22,860
I lost my voice

19
00:01:23,060 --> 00:01:25,480
And the things I wanted to say

20
00:01:25,760 --> 00:01:30,730
But every time I
fell to my knees

21
00:01:31,080 --> 00:01:35,030
I stood up and kept walking

22
00:01:35,300 --> 00:01:40,700
We were looking for
the ideal white future

23
00:01:40,910 --> 00:01:45,930
Our one and only hope

24
00:01:46,260 --> 00:01:48,420
Now I may be left with nothing

25
00:01:48,590 --> 00:01:53,840
But these raging
emotions that have

26
00:01:53,900 --> 00:01:56,940
Nowhere to go

27
00:01:57,190 --> 00:02:02,190
Still, I'll look for a new dawn

28
00:02:02,570 --> 00:02:05,600
With more than one right answer

29
00:02:05,840 --> 00:02:09,430
I won't stop

30
00:02:09,730 --> 00:02:11,460
Until I find it

31
00:02:18,160 --> 00:02:21,750
The Reward for the Death Match

32
00:02:31,970 --> 00:02:32,970
How can this be?

33
00:02:33,550 --> 00:02:35,719
Heft, power, speed...

34
00:02:35,720 --> 00:02:38,020
I have the advantage
in every field.

35
00:02:38,310 --> 00:02:39,560
Why can't I break his defense?

36
00:02:47,650 --> 00:02:49,739
Oh, well done.

37
00:02:49,740 --> 00:02:54,029
I should have taken your head seven
times, and yet it remains attached.

38
00:02:54,030 --> 00:02:57,289
It appears Western swordplay
is more than mere flailing after all.

39
00:02:57,290 --> 00:02:58,579
I commend you as well.

40
00:02:58,580 --> 00:03:00,959
For a man of such slight build,
your technique is impressive.

41
00:03:00,960 --> 00:03:02,789
If nothing else, you
are skilled in trickery.

42
00:03:02,790 --> 00:03:06,499
Of course. You have the
edge in both strength and spirit.

43
00:03:06,500 --> 00:03:09,300
That leaves me only
my wiles to defeat you.

44
00:03:09,670 --> 00:03:12,630
I have also nearly adjusted
to your invisible sword.

45
00:03:14,050 --> 00:03:16,009
From that brief
exchange of blows?

46
00:03:16,010 --> 00:03:20,349
Does this Servant surpass me
so greatly in sword technique?

47
00:03:20,350 --> 00:03:22,059
Now, let us continue.

48
00:03:22,060 --> 00:03:24,940
Show me what you are
really capable of, Saber.

49
00:03:26,230 --> 00:03:27,230
Shirou...

50
00:03:27,400 --> 00:03:28,400
Hold on.

51
00:03:30,860 --> 00:03:36,159
From what you've said,
your Masters work together?

52
00:03:36,160 --> 00:03:38,079
Work together?

53
00:03:38,080 --> 00:03:39,159
Yes...

54
00:03:39,160 --> 00:03:43,709
Assassin guards the gate,
and Caster lurks within.

55
00:03:43,710 --> 00:03:46,420
Isn't it obvious that the
two of them are allies?

56
00:03:46,710 --> 00:03:49,129
It isn't particularly unusual.

57
00:03:49,130 --> 00:03:51,800
For example, you and
Rin have also joined forces.

58
00:03:58,310 --> 00:04:01,639
Me? Work with that dog?

59
00:04:01,640 --> 00:04:04,769
With Assassin, who is
no more than my pawn?

60
00:04:04,770 --> 00:04:05,939
Your pawn?

61
00:04:05,940 --> 00:04:07,359
Yes.

62
00:04:07,360 --> 00:04:11,359
That dog has no Master
of his own, so to speak.

63
00:04:11,360 --> 00:04:12,190
What?

64
00:04:12,190 --> 00:04:13,030
Caster!

65
00:04:13,031 --> 00:04:15,450
You broke the rules!

66
00:04:16,700 --> 00:04:21,580
What is wrong with a mage such
as myself summoning a Servant?

67
00:04:21,870 --> 00:04:24,330
Caster summoned Assassin?

68
00:04:25,080 --> 00:04:29,089
You're saying that a Servant
summoned another Servant?

69
00:04:29,090 --> 00:04:34,760
That gatekeeper there, not summoned by
a proper Master, is not the true Assassin.

70
00:04:35,130 --> 00:04:39,849
She broke the rules and summoned
an Assassin-class Servant herself.

71
00:04:39,850 --> 00:04:44,229
Establishing this as her territory, she
harvests souls from people in the city.

72
00:04:44,230 --> 00:04:46,663
She herself doesn't fight
but rather monitors the

73
00:04:46,675 --> 00:04:49,020
battle through eyes she
placed throughout town.

74
00:04:49,480 --> 00:04:53,030
The three knight classes, including
Saber, are less susceptible to magic.

75
00:04:53,360 --> 00:04:55,893
It's only natural for a
magic-user class such

76
00:04:55,905 --> 00:04:58,450
as yourself to resort
to underhanded tactics.

77
00:04:59,070 --> 00:05:02,700
But you chose to do this on
your own, didn't you, Caster?

78
00:05:03,250 --> 00:05:05,999
What makes you say that?

79
00:05:06,000 --> 00:05:07,999
Masters are mages too.

80
00:05:08,000 --> 00:05:11,289
Anyone who summoned a mage
more powerful than themselves

81
00:05:11,290 --> 00:05:13,629
would be on guard, even
with Command Spells.

82
00:05:13,630 --> 00:05:19,509
Given that, it's hard to believe a Master
would let you summon a Servant to obey you.

83
00:05:19,510 --> 00:05:20,640
In which case,

84
00:05:21,010 --> 00:05:23,523
I can imagine you've
long since made a puppet

85
00:05:23,535 --> 00:05:26,060
of him, like this fool
of a Master behind me.

86
00:05:27,770 --> 00:05:31,399
Winning the Holy Grail War
would be a simple matter.

87
00:05:31,400 --> 00:05:35,779
My considerable efforts are
directed toward what comes after.

88
00:05:35,780 --> 00:05:36,859
Oh?

89
00:05:36,860 --> 00:05:39,070
You say it would be
simple to defeat us?

90
00:05:39,610 --> 00:05:41,830
You, a witch who does
nothing but slink in the shadows?

91
00:05:44,240 --> 00:05:49,919
Yes. In this place, you may
not so much as scratch me.

92
00:05:49,920 --> 00:05:54,340
I shall mete out an appropriate punishment
upon those who would call me a witch.

93
00:05:55,710 --> 00:05:57,919
Not even a scratch, you claim?

94
00:05:57,920 --> 00:06:00,180
One blow, then.

95
00:06:00,640 --> 00:06:04,180
If that is not enough, I
shall leave the rest to Saber.

96
00:06:22,280 --> 00:06:24,370
Too bad, Archer.

97
00:06:35,340 --> 00:06:37,960
Spatial transportation?
Innate time control?

98
00:06:38,880 --> 00:06:42,720
Within this territory, you
can imitate true magic?

99
00:06:45,260 --> 00:06:46,970
You impress me, Caster.

100
00:06:47,270 --> 00:06:50,349
And you disappoint me, Archer.

101
00:06:50,350 --> 00:06:54,150
I sought to test you, thinking you might
be useful, but you are worse than Assassin.

102
00:06:54,480 --> 00:06:56,569
I'm sorry to hear it.

103
00:06:56,570 --> 00:06:59,690
If I get another chance, I'll try
harder to live up to your expectations.

104
00:07:14,670 --> 00:07:15,749
You vixen.

105
00:07:15,750 --> 00:07:18,090
You have a huge store of
mana to draw on, don't you?

106
00:07:26,220 --> 00:07:27,810
Do you think you can escape?

107
00:07:34,940 --> 00:07:36,149
That imbecile!

108
00:07:36,150 --> 00:07:37,150
Oh, crap.

109
00:07:47,330 --> 00:07:48,619
Put me down, you idiot!

110
00:07:48,620 --> 00:07:50,040
What are you thinking?

111
00:07:51,370 --> 00:07:52,789
The hell if I know!

112
00:07:52,790 --> 00:07:57,089
And hearing you of all people say that
makes me feel really stupid, you idiot!

113
00:07:57,090 --> 00:07:58,629
Idiot?

114
00:07:58,630 --> 00:08:00,827
If you know you're
being stupid, then what

115
00:08:00,839 --> 00:08:03,259
right do you have to
call other people idiots?

116
00:08:03,260 --> 00:08:04,260
Idiot!

117
00:08:04,800 --> 00:08:06,049
What are you, a child?

118
00:08:06,050 --> 00:08:08,599
If you're both an idiot and
a child, you're a lost cause.

119
00:08:08,600 --> 00:08:11,219
Pick one and stick
with it, numbskull!

120
00:08:11,220 --> 00:08:12,730
What did you say to me?

121
00:08:17,690 --> 00:08:20,780
Put me down, damn it!
I can handle this myself!

122
00:08:21,190 --> 00:08:22,190
Can you, now?

123
00:08:25,910 --> 00:08:27,070
You son of a...

124
00:08:31,620 --> 00:08:33,830
How does that feel, Archer?

125
00:08:34,080 --> 00:08:39,840
Even the three knight classes cannot
move if space itself is immobilized.

126
00:08:41,210 --> 00:08:43,469
This would appear
to be checkmate.

127
00:08:43,470 --> 00:08:47,550
I don't know which hero
you were, but this is farewell.

128
00:08:51,720 --> 00:08:53,479
What was that, Archer?

129
00:08:53,480 --> 00:08:55,229
If you wish to beg
for your life, I can...

130
00:08:55,230 --> 00:08:56,349
Imbecile!

131
00:08:56,350 --> 00:08:58,150
I said, "Dodge this," Caster!

132
00:09:09,950 --> 00:09:10,950
That's...

133
00:09:16,040 --> 00:09:18,710
I am the bone of my sword.

134
00:09:22,420 --> 00:09:23,510
Caladbolg!

135
00:09:34,310 --> 00:09:38,019
It seems that matters do not
progress as planned up there.

136
00:09:38,020 --> 00:09:42,769
My Master is in peril, so I no longer have
the luxury of concealing my true skill.

137
00:09:42,770 --> 00:09:45,940
Even now, you will not
reveal your Noble Phantasm.

138
00:09:47,150 --> 00:09:51,870
Your Master is a beginner, so you
count on the strength of his luck?

139
00:09:52,240 --> 00:09:54,449
Your trust in him is admirable.

140
00:09:54,450 --> 00:09:57,040
I see that halfhearted
measures cannot break it.

141
00:09:58,960 --> 00:10:00,829
However, that
simply will not do.

142
00:10:00,830 --> 00:10:03,249
You yield the advantage
of higher ground?

143
00:10:03,250 --> 00:10:04,669
What are you playing at?

144
00:10:04,670 --> 00:10:08,169
I may be a no-name Servant, but I
have devoted my life to the sword.

145
00:10:08,170 --> 00:10:10,179
If I cannot convince you
to give your all for this fight,

146
00:10:10,180 --> 00:10:14,060
shall I break open that
belief with brute force?

147
00:10:16,810 --> 00:10:17,810
Secret technique:

148
00:10:22,860 --> 00:10:24,019
Swallow Reversal!

149
00:10:24,020 --> 00:10:25,020
Too late!

150
00:10:39,870 --> 00:10:43,750
Archer, why do you
not finish me off?

151
00:10:44,880 --> 00:10:47,630
I said I would test you
with a single blow, did I not?

152
00:10:51,550 --> 00:10:54,549
You don't intend
to kill me, then?

153
00:10:54,550 --> 00:10:58,429
My objective was this boy.

154
00:10:58,430 --> 00:11:01,849
My policy is to avoid
unnecessary fighting.

155
00:11:01,850 --> 00:11:02,850
Hey...

156
00:11:05,480 --> 00:11:06,609
I see.

157
00:11:06,610 --> 00:11:09,780
You two are quite alike, then.

158
00:11:10,950 --> 00:11:17,829
That boy cannot abide a Servant
like me who feeds on the innocent.

159
00:11:17,830 --> 00:11:20,410
And you dislike
senseless slaughter.

160
00:11:20,660 --> 00:11:23,120
See? You're
practically identical.

161
00:11:24,040 --> 00:11:25,919
How am I anything
like this jerk?

162
00:11:25,920 --> 00:11:26,920
Agreed.

163
00:11:27,170 --> 00:11:31,129
I admit we may both be pacifists,
but that is for entirely different reasons.

164
00:11:31,130 --> 00:11:32,720
You call yourself a pacifist?

165
00:11:33,090 --> 00:11:37,179
You think I'd forget that you tried to
destroy Saber along with Berserker?

166
00:11:37,180 --> 00:11:39,970
That was before we
struck an alliance.

167
00:11:40,310 --> 00:11:44,600
Surely you don't expect me to
try and save everything in sight.

168
00:11:45,400 --> 00:11:47,397
If you follow that
reasoning, even Berserker

169
00:11:47,409 --> 00:11:49,190
would be something
to save, not defeat.

170
00:11:52,490 --> 00:11:53,989
I like you two!

171
00:11:53,990 --> 00:11:57,240
Your powers and
personalities are unique.

172
00:11:58,080 --> 00:12:00,249
Join forces with me.

173
00:12:00,250 --> 00:12:03,579
I have the means to
put an end to this war.

174
00:12:03,580 --> 00:12:04,749
Never!

175
00:12:04,750 --> 00:12:07,290
I refuse to work
with people like you.

176
00:12:09,590 --> 00:12:11,549
Damn it, Archer! Hey!

177
00:12:11,550 --> 00:12:13,129
I'll pass.

178
00:12:13,130 --> 00:12:16,389
Your team has limited
fighting potential.

179
00:12:16,390 --> 00:12:20,180
No matter how much power you
gain, you are no match for Berserker.

180
00:12:20,430 --> 00:12:23,429
What you offer isn't enough
for me to ally myself with you.

181
00:12:23,430 --> 00:12:26,939
I see. Looks like we have ourselves
a breakdown in negotiations.

182
00:12:26,940 --> 00:12:28,269
We do.

183
00:12:28,270 --> 00:12:31,819
Besides, I've come
here of my own volition.

184
00:12:31,820 --> 00:12:35,739
My Master did not send me,
so I have no reason to kill you.

185
00:12:35,740 --> 00:12:38,409
Shall we call this a
draw due to injury?

186
00:12:38,410 --> 00:12:39,080
Hey, now...

187
00:12:39,081 --> 00:12:40,659
I'm surprised.

188
00:12:40,660 --> 00:12:43,869
Your Master has been
hunting me, has she not?

189
00:12:43,870 --> 00:12:46,619
And yet you would let me go?

190
00:12:46,620 --> 00:12:47,879
Yes.

191
00:12:47,880 --> 00:12:52,010
It is no concern of mine
how many you kill here.

192
00:12:52,340 --> 00:12:53,509
My goodness.

193
00:12:53,510 --> 00:12:55,430
What a callous man you are.

194
00:12:57,550 --> 00:12:58,720
Wait a minute, Caster!

195
00:13:06,850 --> 00:13:10,319
Archer, why did
you let Caster go?

196
00:13:10,320 --> 00:13:15,029
Even if I'd struck her down, she
would have simply made her escape.

197
00:13:15,030 --> 00:13:18,450
To defeat Caster, we
must get to her Master.

198
00:13:20,240 --> 00:13:24,449
But all the incidents
in town are her doing.

199
00:13:24,450 --> 00:13:27,580
The victims will keep
piling up until we stop her.

200
00:13:27,920 --> 00:13:31,420
On the contrary, I
want to let her continue.

201
00:13:32,840 --> 00:13:35,482
Caster will keep
draining people of their life

202
00:13:35,494 --> 00:13:38,379
force and will use that
power to defeat Berserker.

203
00:13:38,380 --> 00:13:41,429
Then we'll deal with
Caster afterward.

204
00:13:41,430 --> 00:13:43,679
Tohsaka would never do that!

205
00:13:43,680 --> 00:13:45,219
You're right,

206
00:13:45,220 --> 00:13:49,559
which is why I'd like Caster to
settle matters as soon as possible.

207
00:13:49,560 --> 00:13:54,030
I don't know how many will die,
but humans are mortal, after all.

208
00:13:54,610 --> 00:13:58,360
However they die, and at whose
hands, the end result is the same.

209
00:14:05,950 --> 00:14:08,660
You withstood my
secret technique.

210
00:14:10,420 --> 00:14:13,419
It is not all that
special, as tricks go.

211
00:14:13,420 --> 00:14:18,129
It's simply something I mastered
when I thought to slay a swallow.

212
00:14:18,130 --> 00:14:22,759
A flying swallow will not be caught
by my sword, which is but a single line.

213
00:14:22,760 --> 00:14:26,719
But with two or three lines,
matters change somewhat.

214
00:14:26,720 --> 00:14:29,599
However, swallows
are swift little things.

215
00:14:29,600 --> 00:14:34,019
To succeed, one must strike
repeatedly within a single breath.

216
00:14:34,020 --> 00:14:36,530
A feat beyond the
ability of any normal man.

217
00:14:38,740 --> 00:14:42,449
But unfortunately, I
had nothing better to do.

218
00:14:42,450 --> 00:14:45,370
Mastery through
endless repetition.

219
00:14:47,080 --> 00:14:48,960
The next thing I knew,
I had accomplished it.

220
00:14:49,250 --> 00:14:50,419
That isn't right.

221
00:14:50,420 --> 00:14:52,879
"Strike repeatedly
within a single breath"?

222
00:14:52,880 --> 00:14:54,840
Those blows were simultaneous.

223
00:14:55,130 --> 00:14:58,459
At that instant,
three swords existed.

224
00:14:58,460 --> 00:15:00,049
As difficult as
it is to believe...

225
00:15:00,050 --> 00:15:02,800
That was a dimensional warp.

226
00:15:03,340 --> 00:15:06,384
A Servant who, through
conventional swordsmanship alone,

227
00:15:06,396 --> 00:15:09,180
created a technique on
par with a Noble Phantasm...

228
00:15:11,690 --> 00:15:13,979
Caster is a fool.

229
00:15:13,980 --> 00:15:16,819
She should have taken their
lives while she had the chance.

230
00:15:16,820 --> 00:15:20,699
It would be easier to fight if
everyone in the city was dead already.

231
00:15:20,700 --> 00:15:21,700
You...

232
00:15:25,530 --> 00:15:28,579
I thought we had an alliance.

233
00:15:28,580 --> 00:15:29,909
Don't give me that!

234
00:15:29,910 --> 00:15:32,119
I'm nothing like you.

235
00:15:32,120 --> 00:15:37,960
I would never sacrifice those
around me to achieve victory or a goal!

236
00:15:38,250 --> 00:15:41,629
I feel the same
way, Emiya Shirou.

237
00:15:41,630 --> 00:15:45,089
But it is impossible
to save everyone.

238
00:15:45,090 --> 00:15:50,179
If Caster wins the Grail, the damage
won't be limited to this city alone.

239
00:15:50,180 --> 00:15:53,810
If we should fail, far
more people will die.

240
00:15:54,150 --> 00:15:58,439
Therefore, the only choice is
to sacrifice this city's people.

241
00:15:58,440 --> 00:16:00,899
If that ends up minimizing
the overall losses,

242
00:16:00,900 --> 00:16:03,570
then it's in line
with your ideology.

243
00:16:04,160 --> 00:16:08,700
Saving one person
means not saving another.

244
00:16:09,620 --> 00:16:13,539
You said you didn't want to
involve innocent people, didn't you?

245
00:16:13,540 --> 00:16:15,329
Then admit it.

246
00:16:15,330 --> 00:16:19,840
If you try to avoid killing anyone,
you won't save anyone in the end.

247
00:16:24,550 --> 00:16:26,840
You plan to go after Caster?

248
00:16:27,390 --> 00:16:30,680
Do you mean to waste that
life I took such pains to sa...

249
00:16:29,350 --> 00:16:30,679
Shut up!

250
00:16:30,680 --> 00:16:34,689
I wouldn't want your
help, even if you offered!

251
00:16:34,690 --> 00:16:35,939
I see.

252
00:16:35,940 --> 00:16:37,730
Your dislike of me
makes this easier.

253
00:17:15,980 --> 00:17:17,229
Archer?

254
00:17:17,230 --> 00:17:19,109
You...

255
00:17:19,110 --> 00:17:22,230
Emiya Shirou, if there is no
meaning to your fight, then die here.

256
00:17:24,990 --> 00:17:29,990
Fighting for others but not
yourself is nothing but hypocrisy.

257
00:17:30,280 --> 00:17:33,619
It isn't victory that
you want. It's peace.

258
00:17:33,620 --> 00:17:37,870
Unfortunately for you,
there's no such thing.

259
00:17:39,750 --> 00:17:40,880
What?

260
00:17:41,090 --> 00:17:42,419
Farewell.

261
00:17:42,420 --> 00:17:44,880
Let your ideals drag
you to your death.

262
00:17:51,470 --> 00:17:52,560
Shirou!

263
00:17:54,890 --> 00:17:56,229
That vixen...

264
00:17:56,230 --> 00:17:57,479
She retreated?

265
00:17:57,480 --> 00:17:58,770
Saber...

266
00:18:03,770 --> 00:18:07,739
Assassin, why did you not
strike me down just now?

267
00:18:07,740 --> 00:18:10,699
I was captivated, you see.

268
00:18:10,700 --> 00:18:15,869
You were attractive when we fought, but
your concern for your Master is exquisite.

269
00:18:15,870 --> 00:18:17,580
My admiration stayed my hand.

270
00:18:20,330 --> 00:18:22,539
That is enough for tonight.

271
00:18:22,540 --> 00:18:23,540
You may leave.

272
00:18:24,090 --> 00:18:26,209
You're letting us go?

273
00:18:26,210 --> 00:18:27,759
I am indeed.

274
00:18:27,760 --> 00:18:30,129
To find a worthy
opponent is a rare thing.

275
00:18:30,130 --> 00:18:33,600
It would be a waste to defeat you
at anything short of your peak form.

276
00:18:33,970 --> 00:18:36,850
Or would you consider
this a favor owed, Saber?

277
00:18:37,180 --> 00:18:39,600
Of course, Sasaki Kojirou.

278
00:18:40,850 --> 00:18:42,359
Forgive my rudeness.

279
00:18:42,360 --> 00:18:45,270
You were truly an opponent
worthy of my full attention.

280
00:18:47,070 --> 00:18:49,819
Rest assured, I shall
settle things with you,

281
00:18:49,820 --> 00:18:53,239
regardless of the outcome
of the Holy Grail War.

282
00:18:53,240 --> 00:18:54,240
I swear it.

283
00:19:01,370 --> 00:19:04,039
You stand in my way, samurai?

284
00:19:04,040 --> 00:19:06,629
I should ask you the same.

285
00:19:06,630 --> 00:19:09,879
You would interfere after
I allowed them to leave?

286
00:19:09,880 --> 00:19:12,639
My duty is to guard this gate.

287
00:19:12,640 --> 00:19:15,010
I permitted entry, but
egress is another matter.

288
00:19:15,300 --> 00:19:19,979
Your head lacks elegance, but I shall
satisfy myself by claiming it tonight.

289
00:19:19,980 --> 00:19:23,689
You think you can fight
me, lackey of Caster?

290
00:19:23,690 --> 00:19:25,559
I could say the same.

291
00:19:25,560 --> 00:19:29,279
I sent you to give
the vixen a scare,

292
00:19:29,280 --> 00:19:32,700
so imagine my disappointment
to see you flee for your life.

293
00:19:40,620 --> 00:19:41,960
Shirou, let us withdraw.

294
00:19:42,750 --> 00:19:43,750
Hurry!

295
00:20:02,480 --> 00:20:08,619
We didn't understand anything

296
00:20:08,620 --> 00:20:14,789
My left hand groped for
things that vanished to my touch

297
00:20:14,790 --> 00:20:17,789
A moral conflict

298
00:20:17,790 --> 00:20:20,590
stays your hand

299
00:20:20,840 --> 00:20:23,339
and tricks you

300
00:20:23,340 --> 00:20:25,220
out of your future

301
00:20:25,470 --> 00:20:32,139
I don't know how
to protect anyone,

302
00:20:32,140 --> 00:20:37,940
and my ideals might
well be pointless,

303
00:20:38,150 --> 00:20:46,150
but I want to live my life

304
00:20:47,150 --> 00:20:52,159
The past repeats before my eyes

305
00:20:52,160 --> 00:20:59,959
Here I will trust the me
that now stands with you

306
00:20:59,960 --> 00:21:06,049
Until my dream
crumbles and withers,

307
00:21:06,050 --> 00:21:11,679
I hope you will carve
out paradise with me

308
00:21:11,680 --> 00:21:15,390
Fight your fate

309
00:21:23,140 --> 00:21:24,429
I understand.

310
00:21:24,430 --> 00:21:27,139
So Archer allowed
Caster to escape?

311
00:21:27,140 --> 00:21:29,229
Yeah, he did.

312
00:21:29,230 --> 00:21:30,899
That guy is the worst.

313
00:21:30,900 --> 00:21:34,779
If he's willing to exploit
someone like Caster to win,

314
00:21:34,780 --> 00:21:37,320
he's no better than her.

315
00:21:39,820 --> 00:21:41,779
What's so funny?

316
00:21:41,780 --> 00:21:46,250
Well, it is rare to hear
you speak ill of someone.

317
00:21:46,660 --> 00:21:51,340
But you aren't angry at
Archer for attacking you?

318
00:21:54,960 --> 00:21:58,760
I'm allied with
Tohsaka. Not him.

319
00:21:59,510 --> 00:22:02,600
If you look at it that
way, he didn't betray me.

320
00:22:04,270 --> 00:22:06,600
You are truly
fascinating, Shirou.

321
00:22:07,850 --> 00:22:10,439
Indeed, Caster cannot
be allowed to run free,

322
00:22:10,440 --> 00:22:13,070
but I believe Archer is
not as cruel as you think.

323
00:22:13,900 --> 00:22:15,109
Hang on a second.

324
00:22:15,110 --> 00:22:18,320
Were you listening
to a single thing I said?

325
00:22:18,610 --> 00:22:20,529
You saw it, didn't you, Shirou?

326
00:22:20,530 --> 00:22:23,199
His technique was as
pure as a clear stream.

327
00:22:23,200 --> 00:22:25,410
His heart must
be equally as pure.

328
00:22:29,330 --> 00:22:31,919
He's not that
great with a sword.

329
00:22:31,920 --> 00:22:35,169
He got the drop on me from behind,
but he still didn't manage to kill me.

330
00:22:35,170 --> 00:22:38,380
Yes, you have talent as well.

331
00:22:39,090 --> 00:22:42,260
With enough time and effort, you
should be able to reach his level.

332
00:22:45,850 --> 00:22:46,970
I've made up my mind.

333
00:22:50,520 --> 00:22:54,150
Once I've recovered, teach
me how to use a sword.

334
00:22:54,520 --> 00:22:57,400
Not just for exercise.
Teach me how to fight.

335
00:22:59,450 --> 00:23:00,400
Very well.

336
00:23:00,401 --> 00:23:01,990
If that's what you want, Shirou.

337
00:23:03,370 --> 00:23:05,120
That settles it, then!

338
00:23:08,080 --> 00:23:10,829
I can't screw up
again like I did tonight,

339
00:23:10,830 --> 00:23:13,250
and running away at every
turn won't change anything.

340
00:23:13,960 --> 00:23:17,449
Most of all, I can't let
myself lose to that bastard

341
00:23:17,461 --> 00:23:20,760
who said he'd sacrifice
the few to save the many.

342
00:23:23,390 --> 00:23:26,010
Ow!

343
00:23:26,760 --> 00:23:28,469
We're going to bring
down that magic field.

344
00:23:28,470 --> 00:23:30,179
The enemy is planning
to settle things here.

345
00:23:30,180 --> 00:23:33,599
I'll make you pay for what
you've done, no matter what!

346
00:23:33,600 --> 00:23:34,979
That's great!

347
00:23:34,980 --> 00:23:37,519
This is how
Servants ought to be!

348
00:23:37,520 --> 00:23:39,275
Winter Days, Where the Heart Is

349
00:23:39,276 --> 00:23:41,030
Next Time

